HushGram is the Instagram member of the Hush family of Morphe patch sources.
Its build, shared extension library, settings screen and checks come from
Hushfacebook, which took them from Hushfeed, which is built on
icysymmetra/tiktok-patches-for-morphe, which is built on Morphe, which hard
forked ReVanced. Its fix for re-signed builds and its Open links in external
browser patch are rewritten from Andrew Liang's patches, by way of
Hushfacebook. The notices below are reproduced from those projects. Morphe
requires its text to be carried in derivative works and shown to the person
using the software, so it is also reachable in the app itself: long-press
Instagram's launcher icon, open HushGram settings, then Licenses.

  HushGram                    https://github.com/SysAdminDoc/HushGram
  Hushfacebook                https://github.com/SysAdminDoc/Hushfacebook
  Hushfeed                    https://github.com/SysAdminDoc/hushfeed
  morphe-patches (Andrew's)   https://github.com/andrewliang25/morphe-patches
  tiktok-patches-for-morphe   https://github.com/icysymmetra/tiktok-patches-for-morphe
  morphe-patches              https://github.com/MorpheApp/morphe-patches
  morphe-patches-library      https://github.com/MorpheApp/morphe-patches-library
  ReVanced                    https://gitlab.com/ReVanced/revanced-patches
  piko                        https://github.com/crimera/piko

Andrew Liang's patches are licensed under the GNU General Public License v3.0.
Their files here keep a "Forked from" line naming the file and commit they
came from, and provenance.json records every rule.

crimera/piko is licensed under the GNU General Public License v3.0. HushGram
carries no piko code. It ships the MetaConfig name list that piko publishes for
Instagram 447 (docs/mappings/447.0.0.55.81.json, commit
ea752648f5688a50a96df21430020e98bf9ece00), packed into FlagNameData.java by
scripts/gen-flag-names.py. piko's notice is reproduced below.

